      "summary": "Collect the historical DOCX replay and matched standalone JBMC results",
      "body": "The corrected FSCrawler container reproduced the original DOCX failure and preserving text companion. Standalone JBMC ran on the same original H2 and AWS artifacts as the native checks. H2 hit incomplete unwinding and its isolated caller property even passed on an input the JVM refutes. Both AWS processes exhausted their share of the 600-second engine deadline. Preserve the full per-side outputs and the limits on the comparison.\n\nThe runner collected all three jobs and both independently reconstructed FSCrawler payloads agree. The Cucumber PR record pins the actual merge and head. Both Joda pins passed the 18-input replay again. All Cucumber form, plan, router and cross-example checks passed, as did 36 of 36 changed-test groups.",
